      - uid: smart_vent_controller_frozen
        title: Smart Vent Controller heartbeat stale
        condition: C
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange:
              from: 600
              to: 0
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              datasource:
                type: prometheus
                uid: victoriametrics
              # sensor.smart_vent_controller_heartbeat is stamped by the
              # AppDaemon app at the top of every 120s control_loop cycle.
              # Age of the metric = how long the loop has actually not run
              # (not just "the add-on container is alive" — Supervisor
              # reported the add-on healthy for the full ~4.5h freeze on
              # 2026-08-08, container-alive was not a real health signal).
              # Mirrors the existing Grafana dashboard panel expression
              # (smart_vent_controller.json) which was watch-only until now.
              expr: time() - homeassistant_sensor_timestamp_seconds{entity="sensor.smart_vent_controller_heartbeat"}
              instant: true
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              range: false
              refId: A
          - refId: C
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              conditions:
                - evaluator:
                    params: [360]
                    type: gt
                  operator:
                    type: and
                  query:
                    params: [A]
                  reducer:
                    type: last
                    params: []
                  type: query
              datasource:
                name: Expression
                type: __expr__
                uid: __expr__
              expression: A
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: C
              type: threshold
        # noDataState=Alerting (not OK) is deliberate here, unlike most
        # rules in this file: if the metric itself stops being exported
        # (HA Prometheus exporter down, entity renamed/removed, HA core
        # down) that is ALSO a "we've lost visibility into vent control"
        # condition and must page, not go silent. The local HA watchdog
        # (automations/smart_vent_watchdog.yaml) self-heals via add-on
        # restart within minutes for the common case; this Grafana rule
        # is the independent, multi-channel-routed backstop (HA webhook
        # push + email fallback + covered by the dead-man's-switch) for
        # when the HA-local watchdog itself can't run or can't notify.
        noDataState: Alerting
        execErrState: Error
        for: 8m
        annotations:
          summary: "Smart Vent Controller control loop has not run in 6+ minutes"
          description: "sensor.smart_vent_controller_heartbeat age exceeds 360s — the AppDaemon smart_vent_controller app's pinned worker thread is likely frozen (a hung HA service call can block it indefinitely; see 2026-08-08 incident). Vents are stuck at their last commanded position, not responding to room temp or occupancy. The local HA watchdog should self-heal via `ha addons restart a0d7b954_appdaemon`; if this alert is still firing after ~10 min, the self-heal failed and needs manual restart."
        labels:
          severity: critical
        isPaused: false

      - uid: tati_phone_tracking_stale
        title: Tati phone WiFi presence tracking stale
        condition: C
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange:
              from: 600
              to: 0
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              datasource:
                type: prometheus
                uid: victoriametrics
              # input_boolean.tati_phone_tracking_stale is set by two HA
              # automations (tati_phone_tracking_mark_stale / _clear_stale)
              # that watch person.tati_sharp. The person entity has no
              # mobile_app/GPS tracker (she doesn't want to install
              # anything) -- presence is WiFi-only via nmap_tracker
              # matching her iPhone 16's MAC on the LAN. If iOS ever
              # rotates the private WiFi address for this network, the
              # tracker goes stale and person.tati_sharp reads "unknown"
              # for over an hour, which is what sets this boolean.
              editorMode: code
              expr: homeassistant_input_boolean_state{entity="input_boolean.tati_phone_tracking_stale"}
              instant: true
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              range: false
              refId: A
          - refId: C
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              conditions:
                - evaluator:
                    params: [0]
                    type: gt
                  operator:
                    type: and
                  query:
                    params: [A]
                  reducer:
                    type: last
                    params: []
                  type: query
              datasource:
                name: Expression
                type: __expr__
                uid: __expr__
              expression: A
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: C
              type: threshold
        # noDataState=OK (not Alerting): if the HA Prometheus exporter or
        # the helper itself disappears, that's a separate outage that the
        # existing host_down / HA-availability rules already cover --
        # don't double-page for this specific low-priority helper.
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Error
        for: 5m
        annotations:
          summary: "Tati's iPhone WiFi presence tracker has gone stale"
          description: "person.tati_sharp has read 'unknown' for over an hour and input_boolean.tati_phone_tracking_stale is set. Most likely cause: iOS rotated the private WiFi MAC address for the home network, so the nmap_tracker entity linked to her phone no longer matches. Fix: nmap-scan 192.168.86.0/24, find the new MAC for her iPhone (hostname often still resolves as iphone*.lan or similar), enable/rename that device_tracker entity in HA, then re-link it via person/update on person.tati_sharp. No action needed from her -- this is fully fixable HA-side."
        labels:
          severity: warning
        isPaused: false

      - uid: ha_host_disk_low
        title: HA host disk space low
        condition: C
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange:
              from: 600
              to: 0
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              datasource:
                type: prometheus
                uid: victoriametrics
              # Migrated from HA automation "Infrastructure: HA Host Disk
              # Space Watchdog" (automations/disk_space_watchdog.yaml) --
              # notify.mobile_app call removed there 2026-08-09, alerting
              # now lives here so it goes through the same ack/silence
              # Discord flow as every other infra alert instead of a
              # separate iPhone-push channel. See that file's header
              # comment for the 2026-07-26 near-outage this watchdog
              # exists because of (root fs dropped to ~1.2GB free,
              # blocked `ha store apps install`).
              editorMode: code
